00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:40.660
Imagine you bought XIU last December at $38.50 and it now trades at $34.20.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:46.600
Selling locks in a $4.30 capital loss per unit that can offset gains elsewhere.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:53.500
The superficial loss rule blocks you from repurchasing the identical ETF for 30 calendar days.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:08:01.520
The correct move is to buy a similar but not identical product such as XIC or VCN during the waiting

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:08.540
period. After 30 days you can switch back to XIU if desired, preserving the loss for tax purposes

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:16.540
while staying invested. The 2024 inclusion rate increase to 50% on gains above $250,000

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:22.980
makes harvesting even more valuable. Losses can be carried back three years or forward indefinitely.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:29.080
The biggest mistake is harvesting in December only. Instead, review positions quarterly

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:36.140
and harvest whenever unrealized losses exceed 5% to keep your tax loss inventory full year round.

